build/
target/
golden/target/
*.vcd
*.fst

# The mutation runner is a script, not a package; its bytecode is not ours to
# carry and would be committed the first time anyone ran it from the tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code's local state, and the project's working notes.
#
# CLAUDE.md exists in the working tree --- what each check holds to, where the
# fabric parts from muir, and the mistakes worth not making twice --- and is
# held back deliberately, not absent.
# TEMPORARY: delete this line when it is ready to publish.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# The fuller draft of the project page: the same drawing with the target and
# its block-RAM budget, the fabric/Linux split, a second drawing of the Xbus
# address space, and where things stand. Held back deliberately, not dead ---
# TEMPORARY: delete this line when it is ready to publish. Note that once it
# is committed the workflow puts it at /full-page.html, reachable whether or
# not anything links to it.
pages/full-page.html

# Fetched material: the System releases the processor's second reference runs
# on. Nothing here vendors MIT's packs any more than it vendors the netlists
# or the microcode --- muir's tools/fetch-system-100.sh fetches one, checking
# its SHA-256, and the Makefile checks the same sum again before using it.
#
# The archive lives here rather than being read out of muir's own vendor/,
# because a drive writes its pack: muir's working image drifts under any run
# that opens it, and a reference trace must not depend on a file the machine
# mutates. Only the .gz is kept, and the Makefile decompresses a fresh copy
# into build/ for each run.
vendor/

# Vivado's droppings, from any run launched in the repository root. `.Xil/` is
# its scratch directory; `NA/` is where the processing-system generation puts
# `ps7_summary.html` when nothing names a project directory; the two text files
# are timing-report side products. None is an input to anything and none is
# generated on purpose. Build outputs proper go under build/, which is ignored
# above.
.Xil/
NA/
clockInfo.txt
tight_setup_hold_pins.txt

# A board's private settings, read out of its own linux/ directory: the TFTP
# server's address and the board's MAC, filled into uEnv.txt, the Chaosnet
# numbers and the debugger's pack, written into the card's fpgarc and muirrc,
# and the board's own JTAG cable serial, which the JTAG scripts select it by.
# Private to this network and to these boards; the repository is public. One
# pattern rather than one line a board, because a second board is a second
# file and the one that got forgotten would be the one that was committed.
boards/*/linux/local.conf

# The same, for a board with no Linux of its own yet. The DE25-Nano's names
# where Terasic's resource package is, for `tools/de25_pins_check.py`; a path
# on somebody's machine to a package that needs an account to download.
boards/*/local.conf

# Buildroot's downloads (vendor/buildroot-dl, already under vendor/ above) and
# its build tree, which the Makefile keeps out of the repository altogether
# --- BR_WORK, under ~/.cache by default.  Nothing of the build lands here;
# the staged card and server directories go under build/ like everything
# else.  A board's linux/local.conf, above, also carries ETHADDR for the new card.
